// title: Advanced Feature Disabled · Defender XDR
// date: 2026-10-21
// product: Defender for Cloud Apps
// tables: CloudAppEvents
// purpose: Defender For Endpoint Advanced Features are very powerful, some examples are: - Enable/Disable EDR in block mode - Enable/Disable Live Response - Enable/Disable Live Response unsigned script execution - Enable/Disable Tamper protection The query below returns results if an Advanced Feature has been 
// source: https://github.com/Bert-JanP/Hunting-Queries-Detection-Rules/blob/65d11700e1cb878403d87312acdd6b9a8dd622c1/Defender%20XDR/AdvancedFeatureDisabled.md
// kind: repo
// author: Bert-Jan Pals
// license: BSD-3-Clause (as stated by the repository)
// archived by tools/kql_archive.py (CLAUDE.md 5l, 5eu)
CloudAppEvents
| where ActionType == "SetAdvancedFeatures"
| extend WorkLoad = tostring(parse_json(RawEventData).Workload),
    SettingsNewValue = tobool(parse_json(RawEventData).SettingsNewValue),
    SettingName = tostring(parse_json(RawEventData).SettingName),
    UserId = tostring(parse_json(RawEventData).UserId)
| where SettingsNewValue == 0
| project-reorder Timestamp, WorkLoad, SettingName, SettingsNewValue, UserId
